# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context filter for the Python images (api and worker).
#
# Those build from the repository root because they install the whole monorepo;
# their Dockerfiles live at services/api/Dockerfile and services/worker/Dockerfile.
# The Next.js apps build from their own directories and carry their own
# .dockerignore.  Keep this aggressive: the context is copied for every build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- version control / IDE -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# --- secrets: never bake configuration into an image -----------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*
!deploy/.env.example
deploy/certs
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/secrets

# --- python build / cache artefacts ----------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.venv
venv
.eggs
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
dist
build

# --- node / next.js --------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/.pnpm-store

# --- runtime state: bind-mounted at run time, never baked in ---------------
data/uploads
data/processed
data/runtime
data/objects
models
demo-data/generated

# --- release artefacts (would recursively include image tarballs) ----------
releases
backups
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.sha256

# --- docs and prompts ------------------------------------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md
master-prompt.txt
docker-deployment.txt
progress.md

# --- tests and evaluation reports ------------------------------------------
tests
evaluation/spectra_eval/reports
